    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bb6dd05b_4da25c99",
        "filename": "tools/git-sync-deps",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 138,
      "author": {
        "id": 5015
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-09-03T14:54:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "IMO, the contract is that the script ensures that the repo structure gets into the desired state or exits with a non-zero code and a helpful error message. Ignoring a failure to clone breaks that contract unless we\u0027ve ensured that we did end up in the right state.\n\nGenerally I strongly prefer to catch errors at the time that they happened so that we can fail with something informative, eg. \"failed to sync X with error Y\" instead of something less informative down the line, eg. \"failed to build X: file Y not found\".\n\nA possible alternative is to capture the error, run a series of tests to see whether the repo was actually synced successfully (is `.git/` present, does `git rev-parse HEAD` return the expected commit hash, are there any modified or unversioned files) and if not re-raise the error.",
      "parentUuid": "3e4acf07_b90e7123",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 138,
